  <row>
    <panel>
      <html>
        <div style="padding:8px 14px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6">
          <b>Token methodology.</b> Each agent file logs usage once at the top level
          (<code>tokens.input</code> / <code>result.tokens.input</code>) and re-lists the same tokens under
          <code>tokens.breakdown</code>. This dashboard counts only the top-level figure;
          <code>breakdown.*.calls</code> is the one additive field there. Batch <b>8-21</b>:
          <b>$249.22</b> over 28.2M input / 11.0M output,
          7,577 model calls, 829 agent files across
          24 runs and 3 models.
          <br/><b>Data quality.</b> 105 reimbursement calls failed upstream
          (policy-comparison API 404s / connection errors) and contribute no tokens.
          64 files completed but emitted no usage block at all — recommendation_response (64) —
          so cost for those sub-steps is a floor, not a true total.
          <code>correlation_response</code> reports zeroed usage for all entities while still
          consuming wall-clock time, so its $0.00 line is a reporting gap in the agent, not free work.
          <br/><b>Previous batch (DR_PROD_0702):</b> 841 files, 10,617 calls, 55.8M tokens, $267.38. Kept here for comparison only — those source files are not part of this drop, so the figures above are the 8-21 batch alone.
          <br/>Regenerated 2026-08-31 06:32 UTC by <code>build_agent_run_dashboard.py</code>; re-run it against a new
          drop to refresh every figure on this page.
        </div>
      </html>
    </panel>
